\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces System architecture of DES-ESOD. A high-resolution input image is processed through a shallow feature stem. The proposed dual-evidence priority head (\S  \ref {ssec:evidence}) synergistically fuses semantic objectness with channel-pooled spectral saliency. Dynamic patch extraction routes candidate regions containing high priority to the downstream backbone and lightweight ISPP decoupled detection head, optimized via the object-level soft-coverage loss and scale-aware balancing loss (\S  \ref {ssec:coverage}, \S  \ref {ssec:head}).}}{2}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:overview}{{1}{2}{}{figure.1}{}}
